  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;be two sets containing&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;elements and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;elements respectively. The number of subsets of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>B</mi></math> having&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;or more elements is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>219</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>211</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>256</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>220</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><br />Hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math><br /><br />Now subsets of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>B</mi></math> containing&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;or more elements will be<br />=Total <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo></math>&nbsp;(no element&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo></math>&nbsp;one element&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;elements)<br /><br />=<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><msup><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></math>"
  }
}